@*
    The transport for a drop, and the dialog it raises. Rendered by every page whose printers are
    drop targets, once per page, and only when the reader can upload: without it tile-drop.js finds
    no form and binds nothing, so a tile or card stays the plain thing it is without script.

    The form is the transport and never the trigger. The files are put into it from the DataTransfer
    the drop carried, so the browser sends a plain multipart POST to the page's own Drop handler -
    no upload progress to invent, and the antiforgery token comes along the way it does everywhere.

    The dialog is empty until a drop: its contents come from the page's Conflicts handler, which is
    what knows the printer, the file names and which of them already exist.
*@
<form method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data" asp-page-handler="Drop" class="d-none" data-drop-form>
    <input type="hidden" name="uuid" data-drop-form-uuid />
    <input type="hidden" name="action" data-drop-form-action />
    @* No multiple: a drag contributes one file. The handler still reads a list, because it is an
       endpoint rather than a private arrangement with this script - see TileDrop. *@
    <input type="file" name="files" data-drop-form-files />
    <span data-drop-form-replace></span>
</form>

<div class="modal fade" tabindex="-1" data-drop-dialog aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog modal-dialog-centered">
        <div class="modal-content" data-drop-dialog-content></div>
    </div>
</div>
